WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:06.870
Speaker 1: Remember when the Republican Party
under Donald Trump completely abandoned, even

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:13.010
pretending to care about policy and instead
became all about cultural issues and so called

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:18.130
defending speech and being for speech, free
speech, more speech?

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:25.520
And also when they were against business regulations,
it was always complete and total nonsense.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:32.029
But it is now actually come to a head with
former President Donald Trump actually cheering

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:36.960
Nigeria, banning Twitter and Facebook and
Trump suggesting more countries should do

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.039
it, and Trump alluding to the idea that he
should have done it as president of the United

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:42.039
States.

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:44.309
Whether he could have actually done that remains
an open question.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:49.100
This is absolutely stunning because it not
only violates the principle of Republicans

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.489
being about more speech since these are speech
platforms.

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:58.940
After all, it also violates the principle
of Republicans being against business regulation

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:04.920
because it is outlaying if the U.S. were to
outlaw Twitter and Facebook a legal business

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.469
merely because Donald Trump doesn't like what
he perceives to be the political leanings

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:14.939
of their enforcement of terms of service,
Donald Trump put out a statement in which

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:23.320
he said, quote, Congratulations to the country
of Nigeria who just banned Twitter because

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.479
they banned their president.

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:31.079
More countries should ban Twitter and Facebook
for not allowing free and open speech.

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:32.749
All voices should be heard.

00:01:32.749 --> 00:01:36.929
In the meantime, competitors will emerge and
take hold.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:42.979
Who are they to dictate good and evil if they
themselves are evil, perhaps I should have

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:45.369
done it while I was president.

00:01:45.369 --> 00:01:50.539
But Zuckerberg kept calling me and coming
to the White House for dinner, telling me

00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:52.289
how great I was.

00:01:52.289 --> 00:01:55.010
Twenty, twenty four? Trump asks.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.659
So there there is a lot to say here.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:00.889
But here is the most important point.

00:02:00.889 --> 00:02:07.119
Nigeria banning those platforms has nothing
to do with Nigeria wanting Twitter and Facebook

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:08.990
to just allow more speech.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:15.260
The way Donald Trump suggests Nigeria banned
those platforms to limit this free the free

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.010
speech of their citizens to complain about
the Nigerian government.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.980
That's fundamentally what's at issue here.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.319
So either Trump doesn't get it.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:28.650
Or he gets it and he has the exact same goals,
but either way, it's absolutely despicable.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.790
Now, as far as the right wing position on
this stuff.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.000
Wasn't the perspective of Republicans about
this type of thing, that if enough people

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.930
are upset with Twitter and Facebook for, as
Trump calls it, not allowing free and open

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:47.209
speech, wouldn't people then abandon the platforms
and then wouldn't competitors arise?

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:49.920
And it will all be resolved by the free market,
as they love to say?

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.580
Of course, it turns out that, first of all,
most people are OK with the enforcement of

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.660
terms of service by these platforms.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:02.189
People have not abandoned the platforms in
any significant capacity and the alternatives

00:03:02.189 --> 00:03:03.319
have been terrible.

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:08.010
We've seen Parler Gabb I guess is a thing.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.610
Mike Lyndell platform frank speech with.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.920
I don't even know if that was online for more
than 30 minutes.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.860
And then of course are the facts about the
platforms.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.380
Look at Facebook, for example.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.629
The top posts every day are almost all right
wing voices.

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:27.219
Conservatives are absolutely crushing it on
Facebook.

00:03:27.219 --> 00:03:30.590
If you look, what were the top posts today
or this week?

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.110
It's Ben Shapiro, right winger.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.390
It's Dan Bongino, right winger.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.180
It's Sean Hannity, right winger.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.340
It's The Daily Caller Post, Fox News Post.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:46.019
And occasionally a Rachel Maddow post makes
it into the top Facebook posts of the day

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:52.590
or the week the conservative talking heads
dominate Facebook, and yet they claim to be

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.140
endless victims.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.890
Now, one last thing on this.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:01.829
When Trump mentions how Mark Zuckerberg was
coming to the White House and telling Trump

00:04:01.829 --> 00:04:03.980
how great he is.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.750
And that that's related to why Trump didn't
ban Facebook, although he should have.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:14.840
Trump is admitting he didn't try to ban Facebook
at the time because Mark Zuckerberg was telling

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.220
him what a great guy he is and what a great
job he's doing.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:22.790
So Trump is admitting something which we already
knew, which is Trump makes policy based on

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:28.610
who praises him and who criticizes him and
who is his friend and who likes him and who

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.000
does Trump like.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.350
It's disgusting to hear Donald Trump admit
it, but we suspected that that was the case

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.530
all along.

